I got to a point where I could reach level 7, maybe 10, in a matter of
minutes, hardly trying.  Then I realized that rapidly gaining levels is
not the best approach to the beginning of the game!  It turns out to be
quite challenging to intentionally prevent your character from gaining
levels while still accumulating equipment and exploring.  For me, the 
strategy is worthwhile. 

I suspect from your message that you've reached a point where your
character can survive and kill pretty much everything he encounters, to
a point.  I suspect that point is where your level and the dungeon level 
takes you to a little bit tougher monster than your equipment is ready
for, because you're getting there a little too fast.  

For reasons I won't go into, I take the slow-level-gain approach to an
extreme, often even to the point of playing pacifist, but I don't
suggest you try that.  But maybe it will help you to consider a strategy
where you avoid some fights -- rapidly gaining character levels isn't always a
good thing.

